  "raw": " the world's first psychiatric institute, the primary unit of the new field of clinical psychiatric research, and its curriculum influenced the teaching of subsequent generations of psychiatrists. In 1932, she cofounded the California Children's Administration, which would eventually provide support services for children in foster care.\n\nJean Macfarlane attended and graduated from Berkeley, earning an LL.B. in 1924 and a LL.M. in 1928. She was appointed deputy clerk to the Superior Court for the County of Sonoma in 1927. She was appointed assistant counsel to the California State Board of Mental Health in 1929, a position which she would hold until retirement.\n\nNotes",
  "serialized": "the world's first psychiatric institute, the primary unit of the new field of clinical psychiatric research, and its curriculum influenced the teaching of subsequent generations of psychiatrists. In 1932, she cofounded the California Children's Administration, which would eventually provide support services for children in foster care. Jean Macfarlane attended and graduated from Berkeley, earning an LL.B. in 1924 and a LL.M. in 1928. She was appointed deputy clerk to the Superior Court for the County of Sonoma in 1927. She was appointed assistant counsel to the California State Board of Mental Health in 1929, a position which she would hold until retirement. Notes",
